# A word that adds to a count after the hour of "alarm for 10": "alarm for 10
# more minutes" is a length.  "more [...] Additional; further." and "extra
# [...] (beyond what is due, usual, expected, or necessary; extraneous;
# additional)" (Wiktionary, s.v. "more", "extra").  "of" after a number
# names the whole the number counts from: "alarm for 2 of you".  "of [...]
# (following a number or other quantitive word) Introduces the whole for which
# is indicated only the specified part or segment" (Wiktionary, s.v. "of",
# preposition).
# "h" and "m" after the hour are the unit letters of a length: "alarm for 10 h"
# is ten hours and "alarm for 10 m" ten minutes.  "h [...] Abbreviation of
# hour, particularly when used as a (non-SI) unit of time alongside SI units"
# and "m [...] Abbreviation of minute" (Wiktionary, s.v. "h", "m", English).
more
extra
of
h
m
